course: dictionary
lesson: 1541
title: Words that are both a thing and an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chainsaw is a powerful saw with a motor that drives a loop of sharp teeth round a metal bar. It cuts down trees and logs. Use the words around it to check: «Male lyrebirds are famous mimics that copy the calls of many birds and sometimes human sounds such as camera shutters, car alarms and chainsaws.» The sentence lists sounds that a copying bird might make, so a chainsaw is a thing that makes a noise.
explain: Chainsaw can also be a verb. To chainsaw something is to cut it with a chainsaw. Ask: is the word a thing, or an action? Look at the small words before it. In «a lyrebird copies a camera shutter and a chainsaw», the word «a» tells you chainsaw is a thing. In «to chainsaw something», the word «to» tells you it is an action.
explain: Some words also come with a warning. Chainsaws are very dangerous, so people who use them, such as tree surgeons, foresters and farmers, wear helmets, goggles, ear defenders and gloves. Children must stay well away. The lyrebird copying a chainsaw sounds like a joke, but the rest of the context tells you the real tool is serious.
fact: A chainsaw is a powerful handheld saw with a motor.
fact: The chain on a chainsaw is a loop of sharp teeth that runs round a metal bar.
fact: «Chainsaw» can be a noun (a chainsaw) or a verb (to chainsaw something).
fact: Chainsaws are very dangerous, so users wear helmets, goggles, ear defenders, gloves and special trousers.
fact: Some artists make chainsaw sculptures by carving tree trunks.
exercise: «Male lyrebirds are famous mimics that copy the calls of many birds.» What is a mimic? | A loud kind of drum | *Someone or something that copies sounds | A tree that grows on hills | A bird with a very long tail
exercise: What is a chainsaw? | A small metal spoon for stirring | A tool for painting walls | A bird that copies sounds | *A powerful saw with a motor and a loop of sharp teeth
exercise: «To chainsaw something is to cut it.» In «to chainsaw», what kind of word is chainsaw? | *A verb, an action | A noun, a thing | An adjective, a describing word | A question word
test: Why must children stay well away from a chainsaw? | Because chainsaws are only for playing with | Because chainsaws are very quiet | *Because chainsaws are very dangerous | Because chainsaws are only used in art
test: In «a lyrebird copies a camera shutter and a chainsaw», what kind of word is chainsaw? | *A noun, a thing | A verb, an action | A colour | A number
exam: Which sentence uses chainsaw as a verb? | *The foresters chainsaw the fallen oak into logs. | I heard a chainsaw in the forest. | Her chainsaw sculpture stood in the park. | The lyrebird copied the sound of a chainsaw.
